-- title:
--   Hecke–Galois datum with ρ base changed along φ
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$, let $S$ be a finite set of natural numbers, let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal), and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$ and $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N$ with $q\notin S$ — to the residue field of $\mathcal O$. Let $T_0$ and $T$ be Noetherian local $\mathcal O$-algebras, complete for the adic topology of their maximal ideals, with local structure maps, finite and free as $\mathcal O$-modules, and let $H_0$, $H$ be Hecke–Galois representation data of type $(N,S,\mathcal O,\theta)$ over $T_0$ and over $T$: each consists of a ring homomorphism $\pi$ from the Hecke algebra to the base ring whose reduction is $\theta$ followed by the induced residue-field map, with $\mathcal O[\operatorname{range}\pi]$ the whole ring and residue map of $\mathcal O$ onto that of the base ring surjective, such that every $\mathcal O$-valued eigensystem lifting $\theta$ factors as $\psi\circ\pi$ for some $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi$ to $\mathcal O$, together with a rank-two free adically continuous representation $\rho$ of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ over the base ring whose characteristic polynomial at any Frobenius element for $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$ is $X^2-\pi(T_\ell)X+\ell$ and whose residual representation is absolutely irreducible. Assume given an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\varphi:T_0\to T$ which is a local homomorphism and satisfies $\varphi(H_0.\pi(t))=H.\pi(t)$ for every $t$. Then there is a Hecke–Galois representation datum $H'$ of the same type over $T$ with $H'.\pi=H.\pi$ and with $H'.\rho$ equal, on the nose as a datum in [`GaloisRepAdic T`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16), to the base change of $H_0.\rho$ along $\varphi$.
--
--   This is the normalisation step which allows one to assume, without changing the Hecke structure map over $T$, that the Galois representation over $T$ is literally the $\varphi$-base change of the representation over $T_0$; it rests on the fact that characteristic polynomials of Frobenius map along $\varphi$ and that absolute irreducibility of a residual representation persists under extension of the residue field. It is used in the derivation of local properties (flatness and ordinarity statements) of Hecke–Galois data whose structure maps factor through $\varphi$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_HeckeGaloisRepDatum_exists_pi_eq_and_rho_eq_baseChangeAlong.lean

